+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_VG3JqJi3qbbwZueSQjVVeyC3","content":"agent_id: agent-0\nactual_subagent_type: explore\nstatus: completed\n\n[summary]\n## Verdict: red_causal = **true**\n\nThe D.110c-b RED is genuinely causal for the two intended defects (epoch-pinned adoption, close-not-rebound), executed exactly per the frozen plan matrix, with all should-pass gates green and all red gates explained by pre-existing, out-of-scope debt. One structural caveat (below, P2): this project's \"RED\" convention is an *observation* RED — the focused tests pass while recording the defect — which is explicitly sanctioned by the plan and made causal by the RED→GREEN test flip.\n\n## a) RED failure evidence vs. intended causes\n\nBoth focused executables ran exactly once, exit 0, one test in one file, and observed the exact frozen defect signatures:\n\n- **Node (vitest.json, vitest.stdout)**: test `D.110c-b general hot adoption RED / rejects the genuine epoch-one close at the epoch-pinned predecessor selector` in `tests/phase-6b-d110c-b-hot-adoption.test.ts` passed (1 test, 1 file, 0 failed). The genuine D.110c-a fixture produced a real epoch-1 close with `successorEpoch: 2`, and the one-shot `verifyPendingSuccessor()` (added tests-only in `tests/fixtures/phase-6b-d110c-a/repeat-close-contract.ts:505-518`, guarded by `D110C_B_VERIFICATION_ALREADY_CONSUMED`) returned exactly `{ ok:false, kind:\"chain-invalid\", detail:\"creator successor trust chain is invalid\" }` with durable head unchanged before/after. Token `D110C_B_EPOCH_PINNED_PREDECESSOR` emitted (`.logs/d110c-b-red-7c1e71d2/vitest.stdout:1`). This matches \"epoch-pinned adoption\": the verifier filters for `v3-live-generation-1` predecessors only, so the genuine generation-2 epoch-1 projection is invisible.\n- **Browser (playwright.json, playwright.stdout)**: title `D.110c-b advances one genuine room through hot epoch 0 to 1 to 2 and rebinds epoch 2 close custody`, chromium, expected=1, skipped/unexpected/flaky=0, top-level errors `[]`. After real 0→1 and an epoch-1 send, the first post-adoption `sealEpoch()` rejected exactly **`creator close authority is unavailable`**, while authority stayed at `{epoch:1}` and room id/accepted state and all three retained realm snapshots were unchanged (`packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts:2071`+). Token `D110C_B_CLOSE_NOT_REBOUND` emitted. Matches \"close not rebound\".\n- **Source-shape gate** (RED version of `tests/fixtures/phase-6b-d110c-b/source-shape.mjs`, recovered via `git show 90147e3c:...`): exit 0, all 14 defect-presence predicates true (`source-shape.json`): literal `epoch: 1` projection graph/record, generation-1-only predecessor filters in verify chain/commit/live-seed, `productHasOneTransitionLatch` (`if (successorProjectionAuthority !== null) return;`), `productHasNoPostAdoptionCloseBind`, literal public `readonly epoch: 1`, unconditional `activeOwners.delete(topic)` + lock release, same-bindings stale-wrapper return. These pin the defect in source, not just in behavior.\n\n## b) Gates that should pass at RED\n\n- Passed as required: `node-build-typecheck` (0), `storage-browser-build-typecheck` (0), `v3-room-typecheck` (0), `source-shape` (0), `eslint-corrected` (0), `prettier` (0), `final-diff-check` (0), both manifest validations (0). Runtime identity confirmed the verifier loaded from `packages/node/src/creator-adoption.ts` and storage from `packages/storage-node/dist/src/index.js` under Node v22.15.0 (`runtime-identity-corrected.json`).\n- `typecheck.status=1` (114-line stdout): **all errors are in `packages/object` compact-history-observer test/helper files** (`tests/compact-history-observer-1i-b-red.test.ts`, `tests/helpers/compact-history-observer-1i-b.ts`) — untouched by RED (state-audit TRACKED_CHANGED lists only the two test files). Pre-existing inherited debt, correctly disclosed.\n- `storage-browser-typecheck.status=2` (151 lines): all errors are in `tests/assets/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-*` and `phase-6b-differential-exit/issuance-retention` entries (missing `#phase-6b-*-maintenance` module aliases, branded-ID mismatches) — the \"reclamation-alias/branded fixture-ID debt\" the ledger names. No D.110c-b file appears.\n- Disclosed-and-corrected diagnostics, none causal: initial eslint run failed only on missing return annotations in the plain-JS evidence script (fixed with the file-level disable now in the committed file); initial playwright `--list` with anchored grep matched 0 (selector diagnostic; corrected literal-title list matched exactly 1); initial runtime-identity probe guessed `createNodeAheDurableStore` (actual: `createSqliteAheDurableStore`) after both imports already succeeded; plan-inclusive prettier OOMed at the default 4 GiB heap and passed with `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=12288`.\n- Custody clean: HEAD==ORIGIN==`7c1e71d2`, signed, 27 stashes, protected dirs intact, fixed ports 4174/4175/51000/51002 clear, no ts-drp processes left (the chrome-headless-shell/next processes in `state-audit.txt` belong to other repos — heimdall, freq-ticketing).\n\n## c) Would GREEN plausibly fix exactly these?\n\nYes, and the GREEN diff proves it mechanically. `f2066512` touches exactly the declared owners (`creator-adoption.ts`, `creator-adoption-commit.ts`, `creator-adoption-activate.ts`, `v3-live.ts`, `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts`) and flips the same test bodies: the Node test now asserts `verification: { ok:true, descriptor:{epoch:2} }` on the identical genuine fixture, and the browser title now drives the full 0→1→2 loop. The `v3-live.ts` change is covered by the plan's pre-authorized escape hatch (\"reused unchanged unless RED proves another owner\", line ~94072) and is documented in the GREEN batch-1 diagnosis (plan lines ~94418-94440, `recoverV3LiveReplica()` genesis-vs-anchor selection). The `phase-5e` 4-line tests-only type widening (`epoch: 0`→`number`) is the exact change the plan pre-declared. `runtime-reclamation-contract.ts` +2 lines is a tests-only fixture exposure (`runtimeBindings`).\n\n## d) Vacuity / wrong-reason check\n\n- Not vacuous: the RED assertions would fail if the defect were absent (e.g., `expect(verification).toEqual({kind:\"chain-invalid\"...})`), and the source-shape gate independently pins the defect literals in production source at RED.\n- No environmental interference: no port conflicts, no stale processes, reporter JSON relocated with matching pre/post SHA-256.\n- The one real caveat: browser test duration was 755 ms — fast for a full 0→1+seal flow, but these are local IndexedDB/in-process-server operations with no network, and the defect manifests exactly where the plan predicted (first post-adoption seal). Not evidence of a shortcut.\n\n## Declared scope/boundaries (plan, with line numbers)\n\n- Owners (94166-94172 area, audit paragraph 94051-94071): `creator-adoption.ts:371-373,539-569,607-610,664-666`, `creator-adoption-commit.ts:308-310,432-434,489-491`, `creator-adoption-activate.ts:52-57,189-230`, `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:235-242,453-488,1880-1883,2265-2287,3500-3586`.\n- Public boundary (94086-94093): \"D.110c-b widens only the existing `V3RoomSuccessorAuthority.epoch` field from literal `1` to `number`… The interface key roster, methods, trust profile, live-generation kinds, record/wire schemas, digest and cut/QC authority, room-floor API, dependencies, availability policy, thresholds, workload, and storage schemas do not change.\"\n- Reslice clause (94105-94108): \"If RED or implementation requires a new public key/method, record or wire field, cryptographic/dependency change, authority carrier or assumption, threshold, or migration protocol, this slice stops and reslices rather than widening silently.\"\n- Debt boundaries (94301-94311): \"This slice owns only the hot loop and product close rebinding. The cold-reopen literals… authenticated non-root checkpoint opener, fixed rollback window, pruning, age-independent reopen, and bounded active control proof remain D.110c-0b1/D.110c-c… The multi-transition durable census and fresh-process post-GC memory proof remain D.110c-d; Phase 7 still owns archive delivery and genuinely multi-epoch cold join… Deadline: GREEN before D.110c-0b1 RED and in all cases before D.110c-c RED.\"\n- RED matrix (94109-94148): vitest one-file/one-test with coverage off + the exact Chromium title via `playwright.phase-6a-creator-successor-product.config.ts --project=chromium --reporter=json --fail-on-flaky-tests`; \"A RED matching this frozen matrix is causal evidence even though its diagnostic assertions pass\" (94148-94150).\n- Summary item 6 (92015-92026) and the D.110c-0b1 sequencing note (91849-91852) are consistent with the above.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- **P1 (process, plan-sanctioned):** The RED never fails in the runner sense (vitest/playwright exit 0); RED-ness rests entirely on recorded defect observations plus the source-shape gate. This is explicitly declared in the plan (94148), and causality is independently demonstrated by the GREEN flip of the same tests — but any review rubric expecting failing assertions at RED should treat this as a convention deviation that was pre-ratified, not discovered.\n- **P2:** `source-shape.mjs` predicates are substring/regex matches on source and could theoretically be satisfied by comments or coincidental text; the plan anticipates grep faults as \"diagnostic defects\". Low risk given 14 independent predicates plus runtime behavior agreeing.\n- **P2:** The initial eslint/prettier/runtime-identity/playwright-list failures were all corrected in-run; each is disclosed in the ledger with preserved failing artifacts. Honest, but it means the evidence root contains both failed and corrected variants — readers must consult the ledger to know which is terminal.\n- **P2 (informational):** Broad root/storage-browser typechecks remain red on inherited debt (`packages/object` compact-history, phase-6b reclamation assets). Verified as not caused by RED (