+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_R9WNadNSoFn9fXaaZyTduRO7","content":"agent_id: agent-3\nactual_subagent_type: explore\nstatus: completed\n\n[summary]\nAll checks complete. Here is my assessment.\n\n## Verdict: evidence_sufficient = **true**\n\nEvery load-bearing test claim in the ledger is backed by a manifest file whose stats match exactly, and the diagnostic variants form a coherent, honestly-disclosed failure→fix progression. No hidden failures or massaged results found. Remaining issues are P2 artifact gaps for the non-test hygiene commands.\n\n### 1. Claimed results vs. observed evidence\n\n**Focused GREEN (both verified):**\n- Batch 1 final reporter `batch1-vitest-isolated.json`: `success=true`, 1/1 test passed, title \"D.110c-b general hot adoption GREEN advances the genuine epoch-one close to one exact epoch-two active owner\", run at 17:36:35Z — the latest of the six batch1 files. Matches ledger line 12. (Marker `D110C_B_HOT_ADOPTION_COMPLETE` isn't captured in vitest JSON stdout, but the committed test at `tests/phase-6b-d110c-b-hot-adoption.test.ts` does write it on the success path.)\n- Batch 2 `batch2-chromium.json`: `expected=1, skipped=0, unexpected=0, flaky=0`; the spec title is exactly \"D.110c-b advances one genuine room through hot epoch 0 to 1 to 2 and rebinds epoch 2 close custody\" (matches the committed test at `phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts:2071`), status passed, and stdout contains `D110C_B_PRODUCT_HOT_LOOP_COMPLETE`. The argv records the corrected literal `--grep` selector, matching ledger lines 13–14.\n\n**Retained finals (all match ledger lines 25–28 exactly):**\n- `retained-node.json`: success=true, 62/62 suites, 282/282 tests, 0 non-passed assertions (verified by scanning all assertionResults). Note: it does not contain the d110c-b focused test — consistent with \"<25 frozen retained files>\" scoping.\n- `retained-product-browser-green.json`: expected=30, skipped=0, unexpected=0, flaky=0.\n- `retained-activation-browser.json`: expected=24, 0 unexpected. `retained-live-close-browser.json`: expected=9, 0 unexpected.\n\n### 2. Variant analysis — no hidden failures\n\n**Six batch1 variants** are a chronological diagnostic sequence (17:20→17:36Z), each failing progressively deeper into the test (fixture open → line 21 → line 64 → line 68 → pass), i.e. iterative implementation fixes, not flakiness. The ledger (lines 18, 21) explicitly classifies all five failing reporters as diagnostics, not GREEN. Naming nit: `batch1-vitest-green.json` is one of the *failing* diagnostics, while `batch1-vitest-isolated.json` is the actual pass — misleading filename, but disclosed.\n\n**Retained product-browser variants** (17:48→17:56Z) show a serial-mode staircase: each run got one test further before failing (12→6→3→0 skipped, different failing title each round), ending in the all-green `-green.json`. The ledger's explanation (\"stale pre-verification expectations\" then \"redirected adoption ordering defect\") is corroborated by the commit diff: the phase-6a pw test edits *add* specificity (`detail: \"D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED\"`, `verificationCount` adjusted to the new stall semantics) rather than deleting assertions.\n\n**Ordering-focused:** original run (17:54Z) failed chromium+firefox with expected `adoptionBeforeLater: true` vs received `false`; the corrected run (17:55Z) passes all three engines with the *same* grep and the *same* expectations visible in the commit. So the fix landed in implementation, not in the expectation — the opposite of hiding a regression. The D.110c-b batch1 test itself grew from 3 removed to 13 added `expect` lines RED→GREEN (proper TDD inversion of the RED rejection assertion).\n\n### 3. Consistency checks — all pass\n\n- Commit chain: HEAD `f2066512` parent is `90147e3c` (ledger's \"RED parent\"), whose tree is `03cc689d…` — exactly as ledger line 5 states. Plan base `7c1e71d2` is the grandparent.\n- All evidence timestamps (17:20–17:58Z) precede the ledger's recorded