+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_bZ2squDFFWJvkYUB9SIJ4SSV","content":"agent_id: agent-2\nactual_subagent_type: explore\nstatus: completed\n\n[summary]\n# Review: GREEN commit f2066512 test/contract changes for D.110c-b\n\n**Scope note:** the assignment's pathspec `packages/node/tests/` matches nothing — the two Playwright files actually live at `packages/storage-browser/tests/`. Full changed-file set confirmed via `git diff --name-only 90147e3c..f2066512`.\n\n**Verdict: no P0. One P1 (close-rebind failure has no behavioral test). Three P2s. All retained-expectation edits are documented corrections or strengthenings, not weakenings.**\n\n## 1. Retained expectation corrections — preserved, not weakened\n\n**`tests/fixtures/phase-6b-d110c-a/repeat-close-contract.ts` (+317)** — pure fixture expansion, and the retained consumer is untouched:\n- The retained test `tests/phase-6b-d110c-a-repeat-close-red.test.ts` is byte-identical between RED and GREEN (not in the diff), still calls `openD110cARepeatCloseFixture()` with defaults, and still asserts `hostileCarrierRefusals` length/roster, `overflowRefusal`, `closeAttempts: 1`, exact epochs 1/2. The default path still runs `hostileCarrierRefusals()` and `overflowRefusal()` (`repeat-close-contract.ts:414-417` HEAD).\n- The new `retainedControls: false` escape (line ~414) is used only by the two isolated post-transfer mutant fixtures with distinct objectIds (`hot-adoption-contract.ts:81-84, 91-94`), and its sentinel `\"D110C_A_RETAINED_CONTROLS_NOT_RUN\"` never reaches any assertion. Not a weakening; matches the plan's \"two distinct genuine object IDs\" isolation note.\n- Removed `verifyPendingSuccessor()` had no retained caller (grep confirms only the D.110c-b fixture consumed it).\n\n**`packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-5e-creator-live-close.pw.ts` (4 lines)** — literal `epoch: 0`/`successorEpoch: 1` → `number` in a tests-only anonymous `sealEpoch()` result interface (HEAD lines 256, 260). Runtime assertions remain exact: `expect(sealed).toMatchObject({ epoch: 0, lifecycle: \"successor-pending-adoption\", ok: true, successorEpoch: 1 })` (lines 331–336). The plan sanctions this verbatim (\"widened to the already-shipped D.110c-a `number` fields\", plan doc ~94110). No executed guarantee lost.\n\n**`tests/fixtures/phase-6b/runtime-reclamation-contract.ts` (+2)** — purely additive exposure of `runtimeBindings` on the hot fixture. No assertion touched.\n\n**`packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts`** — three correction sites, all matching the plan's green-ledger (~94490) and the new product semantics:\n- D108E2B \"failure\" scenario (HEAD lines 1095–1105): `verificationCount: 1 → 0`, plus an *added* exact `detail: \"D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED\"`. The refusal moved earlier (pre-verification lifecycle check at `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:3532`); fail-closed shared-rejection (`sameSettlement: true`, `status: \"rejected\"`) is retained. Correction, with one P2 noted below.\n- D108E3 activation case (HEAD ~1843): detail `\"v3 room successor activation failed: authority-unavailable\"` → `\"D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED\"` — matches the mandated post-floor-commit stall classification (plan: \"post-floor activation failure is now exact `D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED`\"). Retry `verificationCount: 2 → 1` matches \"invalid first request plus a valid sealed retry invokes the verifier once, not twice\". Settled sequences `[rejected, fulfilled]` and all other counts unchanged.\n- D108E5 redirect ordering (HEAD 1970–2095): rewritten from a single negative probe (`laterSettledAtVerification === false`) to *positive* ordering assertions — both operations pending before redirect release, `adoptionBeforeLater: true` via numeric settlement orders, `redirectStatus: \"fulfilled\"`, exact stall detail. This is strictly stronger and matches the retained titles \"redirect-pending adoption stays ahead of rehearsal/activation\" (`creator-successor-product-contract.ts:70-71`).\n\n## 2. D.110c-b contract/test: strengthened, not relaxed\n\nThe RED test asserted the *broken* state as causal capture (`chain-invalid`, unchanged durable head, `D110C_B_EPOCH_PINNED_PREDECESSOR` token — per plan, RED passes with diagnostic assertions). GREEN flips to demanding: exact `{descriptor: {epoch: 2}, ok: true}` verify, `successor-prepared`/`active-new` commit, activation with `handle.epoch: 2`/`trust.currentEpoch: 2`, duplicate-commit + duplicate-activation with `duplicateHandleIdentity === true`, a 13-entry exact mutant refusal matrix, old-plane `not-active` issue refusal, and post-epoch-2 issue/publish. The browser product test similarly flips from `D110C_B_CLOSE_NOT_REBOUND` to the full 0→1→2 loop with `closeTwo` asserted `{epoch: 2, successorEpoch: 3}` and authority/accepted frozen pending adoption. Mutant classifications (`chain-invalid`, `stale-head`, `authority-unavailable`, `malformed-input`, `D110C_FLOOR_INVALID`, `D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH`, `preparation-rejected`) match the plan's frozen refusal matrix exactly. Same-head idempotence uses a fresh second `commitCreatorSuccessorAdoption()` capability created before first activation — plan-compliant, not replayed/minted. (Mutant capabilities are necessarily re-minted via the pre-existing internal `createPreparedCreatorSuccessorAdoption`; that is the only feasible refusal-injection path and the module predates this commit.)\n\n## 3. source-shape.mjs — sound, matches diff scope\n\nI executed it at HEAD: all 13 predicates `true`, `failed: []`. It reads exactly the files the commit touched (`creator-adoption.ts`, `creator-adoption-commit.ts`, `creator-adoption-activate.ts`, `v3-live.ts`, `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts`, the pw test), fails closed on missing section markers, and each of RED's 14 broken-shape pins has a flipped GREEN counterpart (latch removal → `productHasNoPermanentFirstTransitionLatch`; no-rebind → `productCloseIsReboundToReplacement`; literal-one epochs → `productPublicAuthorityEpochIsGeneral`; generation-1 pinning → `commitRequiresExactNextEpoch`/`currentProjectionKindIsEpochRelative`). New predicates pin the added machinery (filtered-issuance delegation, one-use recovery-source WeakMap, CAS/retirement-deferral, stall classifications, and even the product proof's `{ epoch: 2, successorEpoch: 3 }`). One fragility nit: `liveActivationUsesOneFilteredStoreOwner` is an occurrence count (`=== 2`), which is brittle to refactors but deterministic and fail-closed.\n\n## 4. Coverage vs. the assignment checklist\n\nGenuinely asserted: hot 0→1→2 issue/publish (epoch-2 `issued`/`published` exact); rebound 2→3 close custody (browser, `closeTwo` exact, authority frozen); same-head idempotence (`duplicateHandleIdentity === true`); stale/same-epoch/skipped/cross-object/cross-genesis/conflicting-binding refusals (exact kinds); replacement-in-flight CAS loss (retirement mutant → `\"creator successor active ownership changed during replacement\"`); delayed old-wrapper cleanup (old `deactivate()` after swap, new issue/publish still succeed); filtered-issuance displaced-source custody (genuinely exercised — the epoch-2 publish path is where the defect manifested — plus source-shape pins); activation failure after room-head commit (retained D108E3 injected case → `D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED`); duplicate/redirected adoption ordering (D108E5, strengthened).\n\n## Findings\n\n**P1 — close-rebind failure path is behaviorally untested.** `D110C_B_CLOSE_REBIND_FAILED` exists only as a source-shape string predicate (`tests/fixtures/phase-6b-d110c-b/source-shape.mjs:84`) and in product code (`examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:3625, 3635`); no test forces `bindCurrentCreatorClose` to fail after predecessor deactivation, so the mandated \"keeps the genuine new active handle and authority, clears the stale terminal close handle, reports stalled continuity, rejects with `D110C_B_CLOSE_REBIND_FAILED`\" behavior (plan Batch-2 acceptance, ~94283: \"Fault cases prove … close-bind failure's honest unavailable state\") is claimed but never executed. The browser instrumentation plugin has no bind-failure hook. **Disposition:** add a behavioral test (instrumented `bindCreatorLiveClose` rejection in the phase-6a harness), or explicitly downgrade that acceptance line.\n\n**P2 — loose durable-head assertion.** `tests/phase-6b-d110c-b-hot-adoption.test.ts:58`: `expect(evidence.durableHeadAfterVerification).not.toEqual(evidence.durableHeadBeforeVerification)` — after a genuine epoch-2 commit+activation the expected head (anchor/epoch/revision) could be asserted exactly; `.not.toEqual` would also pass on a wrong-head write. (RED's `toEqual` was exact for a pure verify; the semantics legitimately changed, but precision was lost.) The field names also still say \"Verification\" though they now bracket the whole advance.\n\n**P2 — retained D108E2B title/mechanism mismatch and classification conflation.** The pinned behavior title \"concurrent adoption shares one real verification failure\" (`phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts:705`, asserted verbatim) now runs with `verificationCount: 0` — no verification occurs; the unsealed-room refusal throws `D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED` at `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts:3532`, reusing the same detail token as the *terminal* post-transfer stall at line 3576 (which also sets `terminalFailure`/`creatorCloseUnavailableContinuity = \"stalled\"`). Fail-closed semantics are retained and the plan sanctions the classification, so this is documentation/labeling debt only.\n\n**P2 — lock custody proved only indirectly.** The plan dispositioned Web-Lock uniqueness proof to Chromium, but the Batch-2 Chromium test (`phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts:2087+`) never observes `navigator.locks`; exactly-one-owner/lock-release is pinned only by source-shape predicates (`activationDefersRetirementDuringReplacement`, `activationPerformsExactOwnerCas`, `activationRetainsAuthenticatedOwnerHeadAndToken`) plus the node-level CAS/retirement mutants (node realm deliberately has no `navigator.locks`). The successful genuine 1→2 replacement in a real Chromium realm gives indirect evidence, but the promised \"exactly one active owner/lock\" proof is not an explicit assertion."}
