ts/fixtures/phase-6a-v3/creator-successor-product-contract.ts:560) correctly still pins `record.epoch === 1` and is not loosened, so the roster is only guarded indirectly at epoch 1. The 137 added plan lines document far smaller diagnostic detours but never record dropping this control.\",\n      \"required_action\": \"Add the tests-only `isD110cBSuccessorAuthority(value, expectedEpoch)` exact-key predicate (and the separate explicit-epoch raw-authority derivation) and assert it against the epoch-2 authority in the D.110c-b browser title, or record in the plan an explicit, justified deviation stating why the partial `toMatchObject` is accepted as the compatibility control for the widened field.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Post-transfer alias-cleanup mutant named by the plan is not exercised\",\n      \"path\": \"tests/fixtures/phase-6b-d110c-b/hot-adoption-contract.ts\",\n      \"line\": 80,\n      \"evidence\": \"The plan's frozen Batch-1 mutant list includes 'post-transfer consume/terminalize/alias cleanup, and in-flight owner deactivation/CAS loss'. runD110cBPostTransferMutants exercises only `terminalize` (source-unavailable) and `retirement` (CAS loss / authority-unavailable). The branch at packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts:395-399 — `consumeCreatorSuccessorHandleAlias` failing after the successor has already reused the stable topic, which must deactivate the raw successor once, abandon the old owner, and return internal-invariant 'creator successor handle identity is unavailable' — has no mutant. The ledger's 'both isolated post-transfer failure classes' is narrower than the plan's enumeration, and the plan's 'the complete frozen refusal matrix' therefore overstates coverage by one named class.\",\n      \"required_action\": \"Add a third isolated post-transfer mutant that forces the alias step to fail after live transfer and asserts single raw deactivation, no residual active map entry, lock release after teardown, and the exact internal-invariant classification; or amend the plan to record the class as dispositioned.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"deactivateOwner releases the shared HeldLock without a current-owner guard\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts\",\n      \"line\": 192,\n      \"evidence\": \"`deactivateOwner` deletes the map entry only when `currentOwner(owner)` is true, but then executes `await owner.lock?.release()` unconditionally in the same finally block. Because the replacement is constructed with `wrapOwner(topic, rawHandle, bindings, heads.successor, existing.lock)` (line 391), the old and new owners share one HeldLock instance, so an unconditional release on a non-current owner would drop the Web Lock out from under the installed successor — exactly the hazard the plan's CAS rule exists to prevent. This is currently unreachable: `deactivateOwner` is only reached via `abandonOwner` and the pre-transfer retire branch, both of which run before `activeOwners.set(topic, replacement)`, and HeldLock.release is idempotent via its `released` flag (line 320), so today the second call is a no-op. The wrapper's own deactivate path (line 262) is correctly guarded by `currentOwner(owner)`.\",\n      \"required_action\": \"Guard the release in `deactivateOwner` with `currentOwner(owner)` the same way the entry deletion and the wrapper path are, so the invariant does not depend on call-site ordering that a future edit could change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED is overloaded for pre-verification refusals and discards the underlying activation kind\",\n      \"path\": \"examples/v3-room/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 3531,\n      \"evidence\": \"`if (closeStatus.lifecycle !== \\\"successor-pending-adoption\\\") throw new TypeError(\\\"D110C_B_ACTIVATION_STALLED\\\")` fires for an unsealed room where nothing was activated and no floor advanced (and correctly does not set terminalFailure), using the same token as the genuine post-floor activation stall at line 3576 which does set terminalFailure. Separately, the post-floor branch replaces the previous message 'v3 room successor activation failed: authority-unavailable' with the bare token, discarding the underlying activation kind. The retained expectation corrections are consistent with the new behavior and are strengthened by exact-detail assertions, but two retained titles now misdescribe what they prove: 'concurrent adoption shares one real verification failure' now asserts verificationCount 0, and the retry scenario asserts verificationCount 1 rather than 2. Genuine verifier-failure coverage remains at the Node layer (tests/phase-6a-creator-adoption-red.test.ts, -commit-red, -activation-red), so this is a naming/diagnosability regression rather than a coverage loss.\",\n      \"required_action\": \"Distinguish the pre-verification 'no pending successor' refusal from the post-floor stall with separate tokens (or wrap the underlying activation kind in the stall detail), and rename the two retained behavior strings so they describe the pre-verification refusal they now prove.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"One-generation displaced-source filter bounds the hot loop to two consecutive adoptions\",\n      \"path\": \"packages/node/src/v3-live.ts\",\n      \"line\": 7363,\n      \"evidence\": \"The successor issuance view is filtered by exactly one displaced generation — `transportHandoff.displacedSource.prepared/authorization`, where transportHandoff is the predecessor's own registration. At 1->2 this omits the inherited epoch-0 row; at a subsequent 2->3 hot adoption the filter would key on the epoch-1 generation and re-expose the epoch-0 row to predecessor validation and publishPending, reproducing the 'admission-rejected: v3 recovery vertex is not authenticated' failure the plan documents. The plan discloses this ('bounded to the one already-retained displaced generation ... D.110c-c still owns authenticated pruning and catch-up before deeper repetition'), and the Chromium proof correctly stops at closing 2->3 without adopting epoch 3, so nothing is overclaimed — but no test pins the boundary in either direction. The filter itself cannot hide unauthorized rows (it skips only rows that pass authenticateRecoveryVertex under the displaced authority with matching digest, author, authorSequence and issued-commit row, and extractAuthorizedV3Vertex requires classification.current so only the displaced epoch's rows qualify) and cannot grow unboundedly (`skipped > filterPayload.parameters.maxEpochVertices` stops filtering per store instance).\",\n      \"required_action\": \"Record the two-consecutive-adoption bound explicitly in the D.110c-c debt row, or add a bounded negative test asserting the exact fail-closed classification at the third rollover so the boundary is pinned rather than merely narrated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"Close-rebind failure clears the terminal close handle without stopping it\",\n      \"path\": \"examples/v3-room/src/index.ts\",\n      \"line\": 3628,\n      \"evidence\": \"On the `bindCurrentCreatorClose === undefined` and `!rebound.ok` branches (lines 3618-3634) the room sets creatorCloseHandle = undefined, continuity 'stalled', and terminalFailure D110C_B_CLOSE_REBIND_FAILED, but never calls `predecessorClose.stop()` — unlike the success path (line 3640) and the activation-stall path (line 3582), both of which stop it exactly once. The shared vote/evidence/snapshot stores are still closed via creatorCloseStoreClosers at session close, so this is a handle-lifetime loose end rather than a store leak, and the handle is unreachable to callers.\",\n      \"required_action\": \"Stop the terminal predecessor close handle (best-effort, exactly once) on both close-rebind failure branches so 'clears the stale terminal close handle' is literally true.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"red_causal\": true,\n  \"green_closes_red\": true,\n  \"scope_preserved\": false,\n  \"evidence_sufficient\": false\n}\n```","ttft_ms":6250,"type":"result","duration_ms":735001,"uuid":"9c624999-69c2-4cee-9ce2-6b8b669eccf4","ttft_stream_ms":1221,"time_to_request_ms":34,"queued_turn_count":0}
